.TH ZERODDS-WS-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-ws-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-ws-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/ws-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the WebSocket bridge daemon binds DDS topics to
WebSocket URLs. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-ws-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the parser that reads it is
.IR crates/websocket-bridge/src/daemon/config.rs::load_from_str .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR listen ", " domain ", " log_level ", " tls ", " auth ", " metrics ", " limits ", " origin ", " max_send_queue_per_connection ", " max_burst_samples ", " ping_interval_ms ", " shutdown_drain_ms ", " catalog_on_connect ", " topics ", " tenants .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr and starts with the
defaults for everything the unknown key was meant to configure. A typo in a
key therefore does not abort the start \(em watch the WARN log.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B listen
WebSocket listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:8080" .
Besides the topic endpoints it answers a plain HTTP GET of
.I /healthz
(200 while the DDS runtime runs, 503 otherwise, no credentials) and of
.I /topics/__catalog__
(the catalog of the topics the client may read or write).
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
A
.B \-\-log\-level
on the command line wins over this key.
.TP
.B max_send_queue_per_connection
The samples that wait at most in the send queue of one connection
(\(sc6). On a full queue a
.I reliable
topic waits until the client has taken one, a
.I best_effort
topic drops the oldest queued sample of a
.I best_effort
topic, or its own new sample when the queue holds samples of
.I reliable
topics only (each drop counted in
.IR "zerodds_ws_bridge_send_queue_drops_total{connection_id}" ).
At least
.IR 1 .
Default
.IR 1024 .
.TP
.B max_burst_samples
The samples a topic with a durability other than
.I volatile
keeps at most and sends to a connection when it subscribes, before its
live samples (\(sc6). At least
.IR 1 .
Default
.IR 1000 .
.TP
.B ping_interval_ms
The interval of the daemon's WebSocket Ping on every connection (\(sc6).
A connection that has not answered a Ping with a Pong when the next is due
is closed with status 1011; a connection that takes no octet of a frame for
this interval is closed as well, which bounds the time a
.I reliable
topic waits for one client.
.I 0
sends no Ping; another value is at least
.IR 100 .
Default
.IR 30000 .
.TP
.B shutdown_drain_ms
The bound of the drain of a shutdown (SIGTERM, SIGINT; \(sc9.2): the
samples the DataReaders hold reach the clients, every connection gets
.I {"op":"shutdown"}
and a Close frame with status 1001. When the bound passes, the connections
still open are closed without the samples they did not take. Milliseconds,
at least
.IR 1 .
Default
.IR 30000 .
.TP
.B catalog_on_connect
Boolean. When true, every WebSocket connection gets the catalog of the
topics its client may read or write as its first text frame (\(sc5.2), not
only a connection of
.IR /topics/__catalog__ .
Default
.IR false .
.PP
A change of these five keys needs a restart; SIGHUP logs that.
.SS tls
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. When true,
.BR cert_file " and " key_file
must point to PEM material readable by user
.IR zerodds .
.TP
.B cert_file
Server certificate chain, PEM.
.TP
.B key_file
Server private key, PEM.
.TP
.B client_ca_file
Trust anchor for client certificates. Setting it turns on mTLS.
.SS auth
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " bearer " | " jwt " | " mtls " (\(sc7.2)."
.I none
is served on a loopback
.B listen
address only (127.0.0.0/8,
.IR ::1 ,
or a name such as
.I localhost
that resolves to loopback addresses alone); on any other address the daemon
does not start (exit 1),
.B \-\-check\-config
reports the configuration invalid (exit 1), and a SIGHUP reload to
.I none
is refused. The reload is checked against the address the daemon serves:
.B listen
waits for a restart.
For
.IR mtls ,
.B tls.enabled
and
.B tls.client_ca_file
are required; the subject is the client certificate's subject DN (RFC 4514);
an ACL entry may name its fingerprint
.I mtls:<SHA-256 hex>
instead.
.TP
.B bearer_token
Shared token accepted in the
.I Authorization
header when
.B mode
is
.IR bearer .
Required for that mode: without it, or with an empty value (an unset
.I ${VAR}
expands to nothing), the daemon does not start (exit 1).
.TP
.B bearer_subject
Subject every connection authenticated by that single token runs as.
.TP
.B jwt
Sub-map for
.BR jwt :
.B public_key
(PEM file: an RSA key, PKCS#1 or SubjectPublicKeyInfo, for RS256; a P-256
SubjectPublicKeyInfo for ES256; the token's
.I alg
has to be the key's algorithm),
.BR issuer ,
.BR audience ,
.B required_claim
.RI ( claim=value ;
a space-separated claim such as
.I scope
matches when it contains the value).
.I exp
and
.I nbf
are enforced with 60 s leeway. The subject is the
.I sub
claim. Without
.B public_key
the daemon does not start (exit 1).
.I bearer
is single-subject; for per-user identities use
.IR jwt .
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving the metrics at
.BR path ,
and
.IR /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9091"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
The key is
.BR listen ,
not
.IR address .
.TP
.B path
The path of the Prometheus metrics on the admin endpoint. Default
.IR /metrics .
It begins with
.I /
and is not
.IR / ", " /catalog " or " /healthz ;
another value does not start the daemon (exit 1). A change of a
.B metrics
key needs a restart; SIGHUP logs that.
.IP
The families (zerodds-ws-bridge-1.0 \(sc8.2):
.IR zerodds_ws_bridge_connections_total ,
.IR zerodds_ws_bridge_connections_active ,
.IR zerodds_ws_bridge_frames_in_total ,
.IR zerodds_ws_bridge_bytes_in_total ,
.IR zerodds_ws_bridge_frames_out_total ,
.I zerodds_ws_bridge_bytes_out_total
(labels
.IR topic ,
.IR direction ;
both empty for a message of no topic and for a sample frame of a topic that
is not configured),
.I zerodds_ws_bridge_send_queue_drops_total
.RI ( connection_id ),
.I zerodds_ws_bridge_dds_samples_received
and
.I zerodds_ws_bridge_dds_samples_published
.RI ( topic ),
.I zerodds_ws_bridge_auth_failures_total
.RI ( reason :
.IR missing ,
.IR rejected ,
.IR scope ,
.IR acl ),
.IR zerodds_ws_bridge_errors_total .
.SS limits
What the daemon takes from a client (RFC 6455 \(sc10.4). A client that
exceeds a limit is closed with status 1009.
.TP
.B max_frame_size
The largest payload of one frame, in octets. A frame over it is refused when
its header has arrived, before its payload is read. At least
.IR 125 ,
the largest control frame. Default
.IR 16777216 " (16 MiB)."
.TP
.B max_message_size
The largest message after reassembly of its fragments and after
decompression, in octets. At least
.IR 1 .
Default
.IR 16777216 " (16 MiB)."
.PP
A value outside its range does not start the daemon (exit 1). A change needs
a restart; SIGHUP logs that.
.SS origin
The check of the
.I Origin
header field of the opening handshake (RFC 6455 \(sc10.2). A browser names
there the origin of the page whose script opens the connection.
.TP
.B allowed
List of the origins the daemon expects. An entry is an origin in its ASCII
form
.IR scheme://host[:port]
without a path (a host with characters outside ASCII in its
.I xn\-\-
form),
.I null
(the origin a browser names for a page without one), or
.I *
for every origin.
.I *
is an entry of its own and no pattern: an entry with
.I *
inside a host
.RI ( https://*.example.org )
is no origin and does not start the daemon; each origin is named. Scheme and
host are compared without case; the default port
of
.IR http ", " https ", " ws " and " wss
and no port are the same. A handshake whose
.I Origin
names an origin outside the list is answered with HTTP 403 and the connection
is closed; the check comes before the authentication. An empty or missing
list: the origin is not checked. An entry that is no origin does not start
the daemon (exit 1).
.TP
.B required
Boolean. When true, a handshake without
.I Origin
gets HTTP 403 as well. Default
.IR false :
a client outside a browser may leave the field out. Needs
.BR allowed .
.PP
The check is no authentication: a client outside a browser sends any
.IR Origin .
It keeps the script of a foreign page in a user's browser from using the
daemon. A change needs a restart; SIGHUP logs that.
.SS topics (list)
Each entry maps one DDS topic to one WebSocket path.
.TP
.B name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B type
Fully-qualified IDL type. Defaults to
.BR name .
.TP
.B idl_file
An IDL file that declares
.BR type .
With it the daemon sends and takes the topic's samples as the JSON text
frames of the
.I zerodds-ws-bridge-1.0+json
subprotocol, and keys the topic's reader and writer when the type has a key
member. The daemon does not start when the file does not compile or does not
declare the type. Without it a JSON-mode client of the topic gets an error
frame (code 415). With it a plain HTTP GET of
.I /schema/<slug>
or
.I /schema/<slug>.idl
on the WebSocket listener returns the file's IDL with its includes in place,
and
.I /schema/<slug>.xml
the XML type representation of the type (\(sc5.2);
.I <slug>
is the slug of the topic's name (\(sc5.1,
.I Chat::Message
\(-> chat/message).
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries frames from WebSocket clients into DDS (the daemon creates a
DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to subscribed clients (a DataReader),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
A publish to a topic that is not bridged into DDS, or a subscribe to one
that is not bridged out of DDS, is answered with an error frame
(code 404, its
.I message
names the topic and the direction).
.TP
.B ws_path
HTTP path clients connect to. Defaults to
.IR /topics/<slug-of-name> .
The topic is served at this path alone. It begins with
.IR / ,
carries no whitespace,
.I ?
or
.IR # ,
is not
.I /topics/__catalog__
or
.IR /healthz ,
and no two topics share one; otherwise the daemon does not start (exit 1).
A bare entry
.I NAME:WS_PATH
(the single
.I :
that is not part of a
.IR :: )
is the entry with
.B name
and
.BR ws_path .
.TP
.B qos
Sub-map with
.B reliability
.RI ( reliable " | " best_effort ),
.B durability
.RI ( volatile " | " transient_local )
and
.B history
carrying
.B kind
.RI ( keep_last " | " keep_all ,
default
.IR keep_last )
and
.B depth
(the N of
.IR keep_last ,
default
.IR 10 ,
at least
.IR 1 ),
.B deadline_ms
(a missed deadline of an instance is the frame
.I {"op":"deadline_missed","topic":...}
to the subscribers, once per period),
.B liveliness_lease_ms
(the lease of the AUTOMATIC liveliness of the daemon's DataWriter and
DataReader) and
.B partition
(a list of partition names of the daemon's DataWriter and DataReader). The
durations are milliseconds from 1 to 2147483647. A topic with a
.B durability
other than
.I volatile
keeps the last
.B depth
samples of each instance
.RI ( keep_last )
or all
.RI ( keep_all ),
at most
.BR max_burst_samples ,
for connections that subscribe later.
.TP
.B acl
Per-topic access control, sub-map with the subject lists
.BR read " and " write .
.B acl
belongs to the topic entry, not to the top level.
.I "*"
matches every subject,
.I <name>
is an exact subject match,
.I *group:<g>*
matches a JWT
.I groups
claim containing
.IR <g> .
When
.B auth.mode
is not
.IR none ,
a topic without an ACL rejects every connection.
.SS tenants (list)
Participants beside the one of
.B domain
(\(sc1 L6). Each entry is a DomainParticipant of its own with its own
topics. A WebSocket connection whose authenticated subject (the bearer
subject, the JWT
.I sub
claim, the client certificate's subject DN or its
.I mtls:<SHA-256 hex>
fingerprint,
.I anonymous
under
.BR "auth.mode: none" )
an entry's
.B subjects
names is bound to that tenant for its life: its paths, subscriptions,
samples, catalog and
.I /schema
requests are the tenant's alone. Every other connection uses the top-level
.BR domain " and " topics .
The admin endpoint's
.I /catalog
lists the top-level topics.
.TP
.B name
Unique, without
.IR / .
It is in the log line
.I connection_open
.RI ( tenant ),
the span attribute
.IR ws.tenant ,
and the
.I topic
label of the tenant's metrics,
.IR <tenant>/<topic> .
.TP
.B domain
DDS domain of the tenant's participant. Default: the top-level
.BR domain .
.TP
.B subjects
List of the subjects bound to the tenant, at least one. A subject in two
tenants prevents the start (exit 1).
.TP
.B topics
List in the form of the top-level
.BR topics .
The
.B acl
of a tenant's topic is its own, also when a top-level topic or another
tenant's has its name.
.PP
Another key in an entry prevents the start (exit 1). A change of
.B tenants
other than the
.B acl
of a tenant's topic needs a restart; SIGHUP logs that, and applies the
.BR acl .
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/ws-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-ws-bridged (1),
.BR zerodds-xmlc (1).
